{
  "provenance": "SYNTHETIC. The first user frame opens a turn that produces an init and then nothing, and the second frame (a message delivered into that turn) is ingested without a --replay-user-messages echo: the adapter must take that message back rather than leaving it with a runtime that never acknowledged it. An interrupt then ends the first turn, and the third frame \u2014 the one carrying the flushed message \u2014 is echoed normally.",
